{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For atonement.</b> For the purpose of atonement — to atone for the altar from all foreignness and defilement. And since it is written ״seven days you shall fill their hand,״ I have only what comes for their sake, such as the rams and the bread; but what comes for the altar's sake, such as the bull, which is for the purging of the altar — we have not heard of, therefore this verse was necessary. And the midrash of Tanchuma says: the atonement of the altar was necessary because perhaps a man donated something stolen in the work of the Tabernacle and the altar." "<b>And a sin-offering.</b> וּתְדַכֵּי — a term for the application of blood given by finger is called חִטּוּי." "<b>And you shall anoint it.</b> With the anointing oil. And all the anointings are in the form of a כִּי."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:39.040765120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}